    "https://jobs.fgcu.edu/jobs/director-of-interprofessional-simulation-and-emerging-technology-associate-full-professor-fort-myers-florida-united-states-6316a7c8-bd55-46e2-9498-2cb275fc61a4": {
      "title": "Director of Interprofessional Simulation and Emerging Technology, Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Director of Interprofessional Simulation and Emerging Technology, Associate/Full Professor - Fort Myers, Florida, United States Home About Featured Jobs FAQ Job Search My Profile Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Ready to Apply? Director of Interprofessional Simulation and Emerging Technology, Associate/Full Professor 10501 FGCU Blvd. S., Fort Myers, Florida, United States, 33965 Full_time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Marieb College of Health & Human Services (MCHHS) at Florida Gulf Coast University (FGCU) invites applications for a faculty member to join the college as the Director of Interprofessional Simulation and Emerging Technology. This individual will serve as the leader for innovative strategies for digital and immersive learning across all of our academic units, fostering Interprofessional Education (IPE). This individual will also lead scholarship activities around innovative technologies. The Director will lead the MCHHS faculty and staff through pedagogical activities including simulation and virtual reality and coordinate research on the effectiveness of the innovative technologies in enhancing student learning. Currently, the college maintains approximately 1,500 square feet of simulation space. Within the existing infrastructure, some redundancies exist in the delivery of educational programming. As part of the construction of the new Marieb South building, the college is making a significant investment in interprofessional simulation and the exploration and implementation of emerging technologies across all MCHHS disciplines. This investment will enhance faculty capacity to prepare future healthcare professionals and strengthen the delivery of healthcare services to the community and beyond. Marieb South will be a four-story facility, with the entire second floor dedicated to simulation and interprofessional education. This space will encompass approximately 28,812 square feet, representing a substantial expansion of the college's simulation and collaborative learning capabilities. Florida Gulf Coast University is a comprehensive university dedicated to quality education, research, and service. All faculty are expected to be excellent teachers; be responsive to changing professional needs; be committed to innovative delivery of instruction resulting in improved student learning; be committed to effective use of technology including eLearning and accelerated instructional programs; produce peer reviewed scholarship; and provide service to the college, university, and community. Teaching assignments may be on the main campus or at off-campus sites within our region. FGCU is building a culture of curiosity, commitment and collaboration.  We value employees who successfully work with others and drive positive change through critical thinking and decisive action.  If you thrive in an environment of innovation, accountability and mutual respect, you will find a good home here. Job Description Typical duties may include but are not limited to: Oversees all administrative operations of the Simulation Center, including financial management, budget planning and execution, human resources, academic resources, space utilization, and operational needs. Provides strategic leadership and management oversight for the Simulation Center, including strategic alignment, long-term planning, mission and vision development, and implementation of organizational priorities. Serves as the primary decision-maker within the scope of responsibility and exercises independent judgment in consultation with the Dean and in accordance with university policies and procedures. Directs and supervises Simulation Center staff; establishes performance expectations, accountability measures, and operational priorities; and exercises appropriate authority regarding employee performance, disciplinary actions, suspensions, and dismissals. Fosters interprofessional collaboration in teaching and learning and leads the development of goals and measurable outcomes for interprofessional simulation experiences across the MCHHS. Evaluates staffing needs and collaborates with departments and entities across the college to optimize resources, strengthen educational experiences, and minimize duplication and redundancy. Evaluates and advances existing and emerging simulation technologies and innovative teaching methodologies to support high-quality, current, and effective teaching and learning. Promotes interprofessional research and scholarship related to simulation, innovative technologies, and educational practices. Identifies and develops alternative revenue opportunities, including grants and external partnerships, to support the continued growth and sustainability of the Simulation Center. Monitors Center activities, outcomes, and stakeholder needs to identify opportunities for improvement and implement changes that support evolving educational and organizational priorities. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Job Description Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate from a regionally accredited institution in a health-related discipline. Certified in simulation through Society for Simulation in Healthcare Certification Council. Experience in academic leadership or supervisory roles, such as Program Coordinator/Director, Department Chair, or other relevant leadership positions. Current rank of Associate or Full Professor, or a record of academic and professional achievement that meets the qualifications for appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. Preferred Qualifications: Additional master’s degree/certification(s) in education and pedagogy. Experience teaching courses relevant to aging/gerontology. Established research agenda with evidence of extramural funding. Demonstrated record on simulation research. Experience with Interprofessional Education (IPE). Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of established skill competency, based on the International Nursing Association for Clinical Simulation and Learning (INACSL) and Society for Simulation in Healthcare (SSH) guidelines and standards. Knowledge of Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best PracticeTM. Ability to provide effective leadership by delegating authority and decision-making responsibilities, fostering professional growth, strengthening team performance, and advancing organizational priorities. Ability to engage productively with faculty across disciplines. Skills in working in a rapidly developing regional comprehensive university with a focus on creating a student-learning environment among various academic disciplines. Ability to successfully develop relationships and interact with external university constituents in construction, business, and technology and to establish relationships internally. Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, mentor and coach faculty and students, and participate in regional/national seminars, workshops and committees. Ability to lead continuing education programs. Ability to deal effectively with a various range of learners and to use information technology as a pedagogical and professional tool. Ability to collaborate both within and outside of the university in the development and delivery of instruction. Ability to collaborate with other faculty to develop a shared vision of the future. Proven ability to think strategically and approach challenges with creativity. Demonstrated track record of reliability, meeting goals, and holding oneself accountable. Strong interpersonal skills and experience working effectively across teams. Institutional Values & Behavioral Expectations: In this role, the successful candidate will be expected to: Seek out new approaches to improve outcomes; remain open to feedback and new ideas. Lead with integrity; consistently produce high-quality work; persevere to overcome obstacles to meet deadlines and achieve deliverables. Share information and insights thoughtfully; build partnerships across departments; communicate respectfully; support colleagues to achieve common goals. Special Instructions to Applicants: Appointment will be made at an out-of-unit faculty rank commensurate with the candidate’s experience on a 12-month out-of-unit multi-year appointment basis with an anticipated start date of November 2026. Because applications and materials are subject to public review and retention under Florida’s Public Records Law, please DO NOT send examples of your project/ scholarship unless requested to do so. Therefore, all submitted materials including articles, disks, slides, books, etc., become the property of FGCU and CANNOT BE RETURNED. As applicable, finalists will be notified of the need to submit specific additional materials. Such materials will become the property of FGCU. Under Florida’s Public Records law, applications will be available for public review upon request. Required Application Materials: Unofficial Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Research including Simulation Licenses and/or Certifications- please submit copies of your certificate in simulation through Society for Simulation in Healthcare Certification Council Five (5) Professional References ​ Review of applicant materials will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. *This posting was revised on September 3, 2026, to update the second paragraph of the Job Description Summary to reflect the college’s current plans for the Marieb South building and its expansion of simulation and interprofessional education space. FGCU is a State University System of Florida member and an Equal Opportunity and Equal Access employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, or protected veteran status. Back to job listing People Also Viewed Student Resident Assistant: Academic Year 2027-2028